<ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">ask</ansi>

Ask an NPC about quests or other subjects:
  <ansi fg="command">ask [NPC] about [subject]</ansi>

For a living follower beside you, safe compatibility orders are:
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to say [words]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to look</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to emote [words]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to equip [item]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to remove [item]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to get [item]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to drop [item]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to give [item] [recipient]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to eat [item]</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">ask [member] to drink [item]</ansi>

Equipment, inventory changes and consumables are refused during a battle.
Conversation and observation remain available. Orders check ownership,
presence and life state again when executed; a moved, dismissed, fallen or
transferred member cannot complete an old order. Anything else you ask a
follower, such as <ansi fg="command">ask [member] about [subject]</ansi>, is
conversation, and the follower answers in its own way.

Members fight automatically: attack, throw and cast orders are refused.
Use <ansi fg="command">attack [group]</ansi> to begin a battle. Temporary charmed
followers obey the same restrictions; they do not become company members.

Use <ansi fg="command">company gear [member]</ansi> to inspect equipment,
<ansi fg="command">company inventory</ansi> for the whole load, and
<ansi fg="command">company meal</ansi> for provisions. See
<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
